&P305860 = YBC 04658
#atf: lang sux
@tablet
@obverse
1. [x x x (x)] x x me3-ka ur5-sze3 gu3 mu-un-ra#-ra
#tr.en: ... of battle therefore screamed out.
2. [x x x] x x zi?# a-maru-ke4 e2-e i3-ug5-ge
#tr.en: ... rise(?) and the floodwaters will kill at home.
3. [x x x x] a2#-zi?# [...] du6 sahar-a tusz ba-DU
#tr.en: ... violence(?) ... sit in tells and dirt ...
4. [x x x x]-e x-gi4#-gi4?#-[(x)] {{da-ik}} za-e kasz-mu musz3?# ba-de6
#tr.en: ... murdered ... you have discountinued(?) my (supply of) beer.
5. [(x) x x x]-a-da {d}nuska sukkal {d}en-lil2-la2 [x x] mu-ra-gub-bu
#tr.en: ... Nuska, the vizier of Enlil, is at your disposal.
6. [(x)] szar2#-ur3 pirig ka-du8-a {{(x)-x-mu}} {d}kal-kal [i3-du8] e2#-kur-ra-ke4 uru3 he2-ak-e
#tr.en: May the szarur-weapon, the roaring lion, and Kalkal, the gatekeeper of Ekur, protect you.
7. [(x)] szar2#-gaz igi nu-tum2-mu {{la ba-bi-il pa-ni}} {d}nin-nisig [giri2-la2 e2-kur-ra-ke4 ...]
#tr.en: [May] the merciless szargaz-weapon, and Ninnisig, the butcher of Ekur ...
8. mi#-tum sag-5(u) digir-imin [...]
#tr.en: [May?] the fifty-headed mace, the Heptad, ...
9. ki ad-da-ne-ne gi4-gi4-de3 [...]
#tr.en: Restoring the place of the forefathers...
10. nita3-dam-mu szu nam-sa6-ga gesztu2 [...]
