&P366185 = CT 47, 63
#atf: lang akk
@tablet
@obverse
1. ap-lu!-ut be-le-su-nu _lukur_ {d}utu _dumu-munus_ ma-ni-um
#tr.ts: aplūt bēle(s)sunu nadīt šamaš mārat manium
#tr.en: Inheritance of Bēlessunu, nadītu of Šamaš, daughter of Manûm;

2. {disz}geme2-{d}ma-mu _lukur_ {d}utu _dumu-munus_ sin-dingir
#tr.ts: amat-māmu nadīt šamaš mārat sîn-ilī
#tr.en: Amat-māmu, nadītu of Šamaš daughter of Sîn-ilī

3. re-di-it wa-ar-ka-ti-sza _5(iku) GAN2 a-sza3 a-gar3_ puzur4-il3-a-ba4
#tr.ts: rēdīt warkatīša ḫamšat ikû eqlum ugārum puzur-ilaba
#tr.en: is the inheritor of her legacy. A field of 5 IKU in the Puzur-ilaba irrigation district

4. i-ta _a-sza3_ {d}suen-na-s,ir _dumu_ sin-ma-gir u3 _a-sza3 a-gar3_ du-um-mu-qa2
#tr.ts: itā eqel sîn-nāṣir mār sîn-māgir u ugār dummuqa
#tr.en: next to the field of Sîn-nāṣir son of Sîn-māgir and the meadow of Dummuqa

5. _dumu-munus_ nu-ur2-i3-li2-szu u3 i-ta _a-sza3_ szu-i3-li2-szu _dumu_ u2-s,i2-ia-tum
#tr.ts: mārat nūr-ilīšu u itā eqel šū-ilīšu mār uṣiyatum
#tr.en: daughter of Nūr-ilīšu and next to the field of Šū-ilīšu son of Uṣiyatum,

6. _sag-bi 1(disz)-kam-ma_ a-tap _a-gar3 sag-bi 2(disz)-kam sag-du3_
#tr.ts: pūssu maḫrītum atap ugārim šanītum pūssu santakkum
#tr.en: its first front (side) is the ditch of the irrigation district, its second front (side) is the triangular field;

7. _1(bur3) 2(iku) GAN2 a-sza3 a-gar3_ puzur4-il3-a-ba4 i-ta nu-ur2-i3-li2-szu sza _siki-hi-a_
#tr.ts: ištēn būr šinā ikû eqlum ugārum puzur-ilaba itā nūr-ilīšu ša šīpātim
#tr.en: a field of 20 IKU in the Puzur-ilaba irrigation district next to (the field of) Nūr-ilīšu of the fleece (?)

8. u3 i-ta _a-sza3_ be-le-su-nu _lukur_ {d}utu _dumu-munus_
#tr.ts: u itā eqel bēle(s)sunu nadīt šamaš mārat
#tr.en: and next to the field of Bēlessunu nadītu of Šamaš daughter of ,

9. _sag-bi 1(disz)_-kam-ma_ a-tap _a-gar3 sag-bi 2(disz)-kam a-sza3_ ur-{d}lugal-banda3{da}
#tr.ts: pūssu maḫrītum atap ugārim šanītum pūssu eqel ur-lugalbanda
#tr.en: its first front is the ditch of the irrigation district, its second front is the field of Ur-lugalbanda;

10. _1(esze3) 3(iku) GAN2 a-sza3 a-gar3_ ak-ba-rum i-ta _a-sza3_ mu-na-wi-rum _dumu_ lu2-dingir
#tr.ts: ištēn ebel šalāšat ikû eqlum ugārum akbarum itā eqel muna(w)wirum mār awīl-ilī
#tr.en: a field of 9 IKU in the Akbarum irrigation district next to the field of Munawwirum son of Awīl-ilī

11. u3 i-ta _a-sza3 lukur_ {d}utu sza i-ta _a-sza3_ {d}suen-eri-ba _dumu_ dumu-zimbir{ki}
#tr.ts: u itā eqel nadīt šamaš ša itā eqel sîn-erība(m) mār mār-sippir
#tr.en: and next to the field of the Šamaš’s nadītu that is next to the field of Sîn-erībam son of Mār-sippar,

12. _sag-bi 1(disz)-kam-ma_ {i7}nu-ra-tum _sag-bi 2(disz)-kam-ma e_ sa-mu-um
#tr.ts: pūssu maḫrītum nūratum šanītum pūssu īki samum
#tr.en: its first front is the (canal) Nūratum, its second front is the dike Samum;

13. _2(esze3) GAN2 a-sza3 a-gar3_ pa-hu-s,um{ki}
#tr.ts: šinā ebel eqlum ugārum paḫuṣum
#tr.en: a field of 12 IKU in the Paḫuṣum irrigation district

14. i-ta
#tr.ts: itā
#tr.en: next to ,

15. _sag-bi 1(disz)-kam-ma ($ blank space $) sag-bi 2(disz)-kam-ma_ {i7}za-bu-um
#tr.ts: pūssu maḫrītum šanītum pūssu zab(i)um
#tr.en: its first front is , its second front is the (canal) Zabium;

16. ($ blank space $) _szunigin 2(bur3) 1(esze3) 4(iku) GAN2 a-sza3 a-gar3_-ri-sza-am
#tr.ts: napḫarum šinā būr ištēn ebel erbet ikû eqlum ugārišam
#tr.en: the total is 46 IKU of field(s), listed by district;

17. _1(disz) 1/3(disz) sar e2 du3-a u3 ki-gal2_ i-na _ga2-gi-a{ki}_
#tr.ts: ištēn šaluš mūšar bītum epšum u maškanum ina gagîm
#tr.en: a built house and an unbuilt plot of 80 shekels in the cloister

18. _da e2_ geme2-kal-la-tim u3 _da e2 dumu-munus_ da-qum
#tr.ts: ṭēḫi bīt amat-kallatim u ṭēḫi bīt mārat da(q)qum
#tr.en: adjacent to the house of Amat-kallatum and adjacent to the house of Daqqum’s daughter;

19. _6(disz) sar e2 ki-gal2_ i-na zimbir{ki}-gal i-na _sila {d}imin-bi_
#tr.ts: šeššet mūšar maškanum ina sippir-rabûm ina sūqu sebettum
#tr.en: an unbuilt plot of 6 SAR in the "Great Sippar", in the street "The Seven (gods)";

20. _1(disz) sag-nita2_ {d}suen-ma-asz-ma-asz u3 _szesz-ni_
#tr.ts: ištēn wardum sîn-mašmaš u aḫūšu
#tr.en: a male slave (named) Sîn-mašmaš and his brother;

21. _1(disz) sag-nita2_ a-na-pa-ni-{d}utu-na-di x _aszgab_
#tr.ts: ištēn wardum ana-pānī-šamaš-nadi ... aškāpum
#tr.en: a male slave (named) Ana-pānī-šamaš-nadi ... leatherworker;

22. _2(disz) {uruda}szen-hi-a_ mi-im-ma an-nu-um bu-szu-sza wa-ar-ka-sa3
#tr.ts: šinā ruqqū mimma annûm būšūša warka(s)sa
#tr.en: 2 copper cauldrons; all this, her properties (and) her inherited possessions,

23. s,u2-lu-sza sza i-na i-ga-ri-im za-aq-pa-at
#tr.ts: ṣu(l)lûša ša ina igārim zaqpat
#tr.en: her pin is stuck into the wall,

24. isz-tu pe2-e a-di _ku3-sig17_ sza be-le-su2-nu _dumu-munus_ ma-ni-um
#tr.ts: ištu pê adi ḫurāṣim ša bēle(s)sunu mārat manium
#tr.en: everything (lit. from chaff to gold) that Bēlessunu daughter of Manûm

25. ir-szu-u2 u3 i-ra-asz-szu-u2 sza geme2-{d}ma-mu-ma a-pil-ti-sza
#tr.ts: iršû u iraššû ša amat-māmūma apiltīša
#tr.en: owns or will acquire, belongs to (lit. is of) Amat-māmu her heiress,

26. _dumu-munus_ sin-dingir a-di be-le-su2-nu _lukur_ {d}utu ba-al-t,a3!-at!
#tr.ts: mārat sîn-ilī adi bēle(s)sunu nadīt šamaš balṭat
#tr.en: daughter of Sîn-ilī. As long as Bēlessunu the nadītu of Šamaš lives,

27. mi-im-ma-sza qa2-ti geme2-{d}ma-mu u2-ka-al-ma
#tr.ts: mimmâša qāti amat-māmu ukālma
#tr.en: (lit. the hand of) Amat-māmu will hold her (Bēlessunu’s) property and

28. i-na _mu 1(disz)-kam 6(asz) sze gur 1(u) 2(disz) ma-na siki-ba_
#tr.ts: ina ištēt šattim šeššet kur še’am šinšeret manā lubūšam
#tr.en: every year: 1.800 litres of barley, 12 minas of clothing allowance,

29. _2(ban2) 4(disz) sila3 i3-ba 6(disz) ezem-hi-a 2(ban2) zi3-da-hi-a_
#tr.ts: šitta šât ešret qa piššatam šeššet isinnī šitta šât qēmam
#tr.en: 24 litres of oil allotment, 6 "isinnu" food portions, 20 litres of flour,

30. _2(disz) uzu-ta-a_ {disz}geme2-{d}ma-mu _lukur_ {d}utu dumu-munus_ sin-dingir i-pa-aq-qi2-si
#tr.ts: šinā šīrī amat-māmu nadīt šamaš mārat sîn-ilī ipaqqi(s)si
#tr.en: 2 thigh-cuts of meat, Amat-māmu nadītu of Šamaš daughter of Sîn-ilī will provide her.

31. _2/3(disz) ma-na 6(disz) gin2 ku3-babbar_ hu-bu-li {disz}be-le-su2-nu
#tr.ts: šinip manā šeššet šiqil kaspam ḫubu(l)li bēle(s)sunu
#tr.en: 46 shekels of silver, a debt of Bēlessunu,

32. {disz}geme2-{d}ma-mu _dumu-munus_ sin-dingir i-pu-ul
#tr.ts: amat-māmu mārat sîn-ilī īpul
#tr.en: Amat-māmu daughter of Sîn-ilī paid (so)

33. {disz}be-le-su2-nu u2-ul ih-ta-ba-al
#tr.ts: bēle(s)sunu ul iḫtabal
#tr.en: Bēlessunu is no (more) in debt.

34. mi-im-mu-sza an-nu-um a-na hu-bu-li-sza u2-ul iz-za-az
#tr.ts: mimmûša annûm ana ḫubu(l)līša ul izzaz
#tr.en: All her (aforementioned) property will not be liable for her debt (and)

35. sza sze-a-am u3 _ku3-babbar_ i-qi2-pu-szi i-na mi-im-mu-sza i-te-el-li
#tr.ts: ša še’am ū kaspam iqi(p)pūši ina mimmûša ītelli
#tr.en: whoever would lend barley or silver to her, would have no right to (lit. will forfeit) her property.

36. isz-tu be-le-su2-nu ap-lu-sa3 an-ni-tam a-na geme2-{d}ma-mu
#tr.ts: ištu bēle(s)sunu aplū(s)sa annîtam ana amat-māmu
#tr.en: After Bēlessunu this inheritance (lit. of her) to Amat-māmu

37. _dumu-munus_ sin-dingir id-di-nu-ma _mu 2(disz)-kam_ i-pe2-ru-szi
#tr.ts: mārat sîn-ilī iddinūma šittā šanātim īpirūši
#tr.en: daughter of Sîn-ilī gave and supported her for two years,

38. {disz}geme2-{d}utu _dumu-munus_ i3-li2-i-qi2-sza {disz}ni-szi-i-ni-szu _dumu-munus_ dingir-pi2-{d}utu
#tr.ts: amat-šamaš mārat ilī-iqīša(m) nīši-īnīšu mārat anum-pî-šamaš
#tr.en: Amat-šamaš daughter of Ilī-iqīšam (and) Nīši-īnīšu daughter of Anum-pî-šamaš,

39. _dumu-munus-mesz_ a-ah-hi a-bi-sza a-na _a-sza3_-am sza pi2-i t,up-pi2
#expected _a-sza3_-im
#tr.ts: mārāt aḫḫī abīša ana eqlim ša pî ṭuppi(m)
#tr.en: her (of Bēlessunu) cousins (lit. the daughters of her father’s brothers), for the field(s) which are reported in this tablet,

40. an-ni-im ir-gu-ma-ma# t,up-pa-at nu-du-ni {disz}be-le-su2-nu
#tr.ts: annîm irgumāma ṭuppāt nudu(n)nî bēle(s)sunu
#tr.en: raised a claim. The tablets concerning (lit. of) the dowry of Bēlessunu,

41. sza a-bu-sza id-di-nu-szi-im t,up-pa-at ap-lu-ut
#tr.ts: ša abūša iddinūšim ṭuppāt aplūt
#tr.en: which her father had given her, the inheritance tablets of

42. {disz}na-ra-am-tum a-ha-at a-bi-sza
#tr.ts: narāmtum aḫat abīša
#tr.en: Narāmtum her aunt (lit. her father’s sister),

@reverse
1. sza ap-lu-sa3 id-di-nu-szi-im-ma ma-li _sza3_ sza ma-s,i2-a-at
#tr.ts: ša aplū(s)sa iddinūšimma mali libbi ša maṣiat
#tr.en: whose inheritance she had given her to use as she wished,

2. u3 t,up-pa-at _dumu-munus-mesz_ ah-hi a-bi-sza sza ir-gu-ma-szi-im
#tr.ts: u ṭuppāt mārāt aḫḫī abīša irgumāšim
#tr.en: and the tablets of her cousins who sued her,

3. {disz}zi-im-ri-e-ra-ah ra-bi-a-an zimbir{ki}
#tr.ts: zimri-eraḫ rabiān sippir
#tr.en: Zimri-eraḫ, the mayor of Sippar,

4. u3 _kar_ zimbir{ki} i-na _ka2_ {d}utu i-mu-ru-ma
#tr.ts: u kār sippir ina bāb šamaš īmurūma
#tr.en: and the kārum body of Sippar examined at the gate of Šamaš and,

5. a-na pi2-i t,up-pa-ti-sza mi-im-ma-sza an-ni-a-am u2-bi-ir-ru-ma
#tr.ts: ana pî ṭuppātīša mimmâša annîam ubirrūma
#tr.en: according to the content of her tablets, they confirmed all her estate and

6. a-na be-le-su2-nu id-di-nu asz-szum geme2-{d}utu u3 ni-szi-i-ni-szu
#tr.ts: ana bēle(s)sunu iddinū aššum amat-šamaš u nīši-īnīšu
#tr.en: gave (it) to Bēlessunu. Because Amat-šamaš and Nīši-īnīšu

7. i-na la i-di-im ir-gu-ma-szi-im sze-er-tam i-mi-du-szi-na-ti
#tr.ts: ina la idim irgumāšim šertam īmidūšināti
#tr.en: brought a suit against her whitout grounds, (the judges) imposed a penalty to them

8. u3 t,up-pi2 la ra-ga-mi-im u2-sze-zi-bu-szi-na-ti
#tr.ts: u ṭuppi la ragamim ušezibūšināti
#tr.en: and had them make out a no-claim tablet.

9. isz-tu t,up-pi2 la ra-ga-mi-im u2-sze-zi-bu-szi-na-ti
#tr.ts: ištu ṭuppi la ragamim ušezibūšināti
#tr.en: After (the judges) had them make out the no-claim tablet,

10. u3 be-le-su2-nu a-na szi-ma-ti-sza il-li-ku
#tr.ts: u bēle(s)sunu ana šimatīša illiku
#tr.en: and Bēlessunu died (lit. went to her fate),

11. t,up-pi2 ap-lu-tim t,up-pa-at um-ma-tim sza _a-sza3_-im u3 _e2_
#tr.ts: ṭuppi aplūtim ṭuppāt ummatim ša eqlim u bītim
#tr.en: the tablet of inheritance, the original tablets concerning the field(s) and the house

12. sza be-le-su2-nu a-na geme2-{d}ma-mu _dumu-munus_ sin-dingir id-di-nu
#tr.ts: ša bēle(s)sunu ana amat-māmu mārat sîn-ilī iddinu
#tr.en: that Bēlessunu had given to Amat-māmu daughter of Sîn-ilī

13. u3 t,up-pi2 la ra-ga-mi-im sza _dumu-munus-mesz ah-hi a-bi-sza szu-zu-ba
#tr.ts: u ṭuppi la ragamim ša mārāt aḫḫī abīša šuzubā
#tr.en: as well as the no-claim tablet that her cousins had had to leave,

14. {disz}{d}suen-dingir [a]-na ma-s,a-ar-tim i-na _e2_ i-ku-un#-pi4-sin a-hi-sza i-zi-ba
#tr.ts: sîn-ilī ana ma(ṣ)ṣartim ina bīt ikūn-pî-sîn aḫīša īziba(m)
#tr.en: Sîn-ilī brought into the house of Ikūn-pî-sîn his brother for safekeeping.

15. t,up-pa-tum szi-na i-na _e2_ i-ku-un-pi4-sin ih-li-qa2-ma
#tr.ts: ṭuppātum šina ina bīt ikūn-pî-sîn iḫliqāma
#tr.en: These tablets were lost in the house of Ikūn-pî-sîn so

16. {disz}sin-dingir ma-har sin-isz-me-a-ni u3 _kar zimbir{ki}_ isz-ku-ma
#tr.ts: sîn-ilī maḫar sîn-išmea(n)ni u kār sippir išku(m)ma
#tr.en: Sîn-ilī has made a statement before Sîn-išmeanni and the kāru body of Sippar and

17. i-ku-un-pi4-sin ki-ma t,up-pa-tum szi-na hal-qa2-a
#tr.ts: ikūn-pî-sîn kīma ṭuppātum šina ḫalqā
#tr.en: Ikūn-pî-sîn: "These tablets have been lost!"

18. [a]-na# sin-[isz]-me-a-ni u3 _kar_ zimbir{ki} iq-bi
#tr.ts: ana sîn-išmea(n)ni u kār sippir iqbi
#tr.en: has said to Sîn-išmeanni and the kāru body of Sippar.

