#tr.en: and had them make out a no-claim tablet.

7. isz-tu t,up-pi2 la ra-ga-mi-im u2-sze-zi-bu-szi-na-ti
#tr.ts: ištu ṭuppi la ragamim ušezibūšināti
#tr.en: After (the judges) had them make out the no-claim tablet,

8. u3 be-le-su2-nu a-na szi-ma-ti-sza il-li-ku
#tr.ts: u bēle(s)sunu ana šimatīša illiku
#tr.en: and Bēlessunu died,

9. t,up-pi2 ap-lu-tim t,up-pa-at um-ma-tim sza _a-sza3 u3 e2_
#tr.ts: ṭuppi aplūtim ṭuppāt ummatim ša eqlim u bītim
#tr.en: the tablet of inheritance, the original tablets concerning the field(s) and the house

10. sza be-le-su2-nu a-na a-ma-at-{d}ma-mu _dumu-munus_ sin-dingir id-di-nu
#tr.ts: ša bēle(s)sunu ana amat-māmu mārat sîn-ilī iddinu
#tr.en: that Bēlessunu had given to Amat-māmu daughter of Sîn-ilī

11. u3 t,up-pi2 la ra-ga-mi-im sza _dumu-munus-mesz ah-hi a-bi-sza szu-zu-ba
#tr.ts: u ṭuppi la ragamim ša mārāt aḫḫī abīša šuzubā
#tr.en: as well as the no-claim tablet that her cousins had had to leave,

12. {disz}{d}suen-dingir a-na _e2_ i-ku-un-pi4-{d}suen# a-hi-sza
#tr.ts: sîn-ilī ana bīt ikūn-pî-sîn ahīša
#tr.en: Sîn-ilī into the house of Ikūn-pî-sîn his brother

13. a-na ma-s,a-ar-tim i-zi-ba t,up-[pa-tum szi-na]
#tr.ts: ana ma(ṣ)ṣartim īziba(m) ṭuppātum šina
#tr.en: brought for safekeeping. These tablets

14. i-na _e2_ i-ku-un-pi4-{d}suen ih-li#-[qa2-ma]
#tr.ts: ina bīt ikūn-pî-sîn iḫliqāma
#tr.en: were lost in the house of Ikūn-pî-sîn so

15. {disz}sin-dingir ma-har {d}suen-isz-me-[a-ni]
#tr.ts: sîn-ilī maḫar sîn-ismea(n)ni
#tr.en: Sîn-ilī before Sîn-išmeanni

16. u3 _kar zimbir{ki}_ isz-ku-ma# [ki-ma t,up-pa-tum szi-na hal-qa2-a]
#tr.ts: u kār sippir išku(m)ma kīma ṭuppātum šina ḫalqā
#tr.en: and the kāru body of Sippar has made a statement and: "These tablets have been lost!"

17. i-ku-un-pi4-{d}suen a-na {d}suen#-[isz-me-a-ni u3 _kar_ zimbir{ki} iq-bi]
#tr.ts: ikūn-pî-sîn ana sîn-ismeanni u kār sippir iqbi
#tr.en: Ikūn-pî-sîn has said to Sîn-išmeanni and the kāru body of Sippar.

18. [i]-na# qa2-be2-e {disz}{d}suen-isz-me-a-[ni u3 _kar_ zimbir{ki}]
#tr.ts: ina qabê sîn-ismeanni u kār sippir
#tr.en: By order of Sîn-išmeanni and the kāru body of Sippar,

19. [t,up]-pa-szu an-ni-a-am a-na pi2-i szi-[bu-tim u2-ba-al-li-t,u2-ma]
#tr.ts: ṭuppašu annîam ana pî šībūtim uballiṭūma
#tr.en: they have let this relevant tablet drawn up according to the testimony of the witnesses so (if)
#For ṭuppa-šu, see K. R. Veenhof in "Figurative Language in the Ancient Near East" London, 1987 p. 62 n. 31.

20. [t,up]-pi2 ap-lu-tim t,up-pa-at um-[ma-tim u3 t,up-pi2 la ra-ga-mi-im]
#tr.ts: ṭuppi aplūtim ṭuppāt ummatim u ṭuppi la ragamim
#tr.en: the tablet of inheritance, the original tablets and the no-claim tablet,

21. [sza] a-ma-at-{d}ma-mu _dumu-munus_ {d}suen#-[dingir it-ti be-le-su2-nu la-qi2-a-at]
#tr.ts: ša amat-māmu mārat sîn-ilî itti bēle(s)sunu laqiat
#tr.en: which Amat-māmu daughter of Sîn-ilī acquired from Bēlessunu,

22. [i]-na# _e2_ i-ku-un-pi4-{d}suen [u3 e-ma in-nam-ma-ra]
#tr.ts: ina bīt ikūn-pî-sîn u ēma innammarā
#tr.en: should be found in Ikūn-pî-sîn’s house or wherever,

23. [sza] a-ma-at-{d}ma-mu-ma# [_dumu-munus_ {d}suen-dingir ...]
#tr.ts: ša amat-māmūma mārat sîn-ilī
#tr.en: are of Amat-māmu daughter of Sîn-ilī alone

