&P382523 = CT 02, pl. 41, Bu 1891-05-09, 410 
#atf: lang akk 
@tablet 
@obverse 
1. _ibila#_ sza-at-{d}a-a _lukur utu_ dumu-munus_ {d}utu#-dingir 
#tr.it: Eredità di Šat-ayya, naditu di Šamaš, figlia di Šamaš-ilum;
2. {disz}a-ma-at-{d}ma-mu _lukur utu dumu-munus_ sza-i3-li2-szu 
#tr.it: Amat-mamu naditu di Šamaš, figlia di Ša-ilišu
3. re-di-it wa-ar-ka-ti-sza 
#tr.it: (è) l'erede delle sue proprietà:
4. _1(esze3) GAN2 a-sza3_ i-na ga-mi-na-nu-um   
#tr.it: un eblu di terreno a Gaminanum,
5. i-ta _a-sza3_ {d}i-ku!-nu-um-qa2-zu  
#tr.it: vicino al campo di Imanum-qa(s)su
6. u3 i-ta _a-sza3_ a-hu-ni! _dumu_ a-ab-ba 
#tr.it: e vicino al campo di Aḫuni figlio di Abba,
7. _1/2(disz) sar e2-du3!-a_ i-na ga-gi-im 
#tr.it: una costruzione di mezzo sar nel convento
8. _da e2_ mu-ha-ad-di-tum _dumu-munus_ ab-di-im 
#tr.it: vicino alla casa di Muḫadditum figlia di Abdim,
9. mi-im-ma an-ni-im 
#tr.it: (è) Tutto ciò
10. sza sza-at-{d}a-a _lukur utu_ um-ma-sza 
#tr.it: che Šat-ayya, naditu di Šamaš sua madre,
11. a-na a-ma-at-{d}ma-mu _dumu-munus_ sza-i3-li2-szu id-di-in 
#tr.it: ad Amat-mamu figlia di Ša-ilišu ha dato.
12. 3(iku) _GAN2 a-sza3_ ta-wi-ir-tum i-na ga-mi-na-nu-um 
#tr.it: 3 iku di terreno irrigato a Gaminanum
13. i-ta _a-sza3_ {d}suen-re-me-ni 
#tr.it: vicino al campo di Sin-remeni
14. u3 i-ta _a-sza3_ na-bi-{d}utu 
#tr.it: e vicino al campo di Nabi-Šamaš,
@reverse 
1. _1(disz) sag geme2_ i3-li2-dum-qi2!(DI) 
#tr.it: una schiava (di nome) Ili-dumqi,
2. _1(disz) sag geme2_ be-el-ti-ma-le-e  
#tr.it: una schiava (di nome) Bel-timale,
3. _1(disz) sag geme2_ {d}ur-ki-tum-la-ma-si2 
#tr.it: una schiava (di nome) Urkitum-lama(s)si,
4. _1(disz) ab2 6(disz) u8-udu-hi-a_ 
#tr.it: una vacca, sei pecore,
5. mi-im-ma an-ni-im sza-i3-li2-szu a-bu-sza 
#tr.it: tutto ciò Ša-ilišu, suo padre,
6. u3 sza-mu-uh-tum um-ma-sza 
#tr.it: e Šamuḫtum, sua madre,
7. a-na a-ma-at-{d}ma-mu ma-ar-ti-szu-nu id-di#-nu 
#tr.it: ad Amat-mamu, loro figlia, hanno donato.
8. i-na ah-hi-sza a-na sza ta-ra-mu-u2 
#tr.it: Tra i suoi fratelli, a quello che preferisce,
9. ap-lu!-sa3 i-na-di-in 
#tr.it: la sua eredità lascerà (lit. darà).
10. a-di sza-at-{d}a-a _dumu-munus_ {d}utu!-dingir!  
#tr.it: Finché Šat-ayya, figlia di Šamaš-ilum,
11. ba-al-t,a3-at i-na _mu 1(disz)-kam_ 
#tr.it: sarà in vita, ogni anno
12. _1(disz) gin2! ku3-babbar siki-ba 6(disz) sila3 i3-ba_ 
#tr.it: 1 siclo di argento in abiti, 6 litri d'olio,
13. _4(disz) ezem {d}utu 2(ban2) zi3!-da 1(disz) uzu!-ta-am3 2(disz) sze_  
#tr.it: 4 porzioni, in occasione delle feste di Šamaš, (composte da): 2 seah di farina, 1 (pezzo di) carne, e due litri d'orzo 
14. {disz}a-ma-at-{d}ma-mu it-ta-na-di-szi-im  
#tr.it: Amat-mamu le darà.
15. _mu_ {d}utu {d}a-a {d}amar-utu u3 ha-am-mu-ra-pi2 _in-pa3-de3-mesz_ 
#tr.it: Sul nome di Šamaš, Ayya, Marduk e Ḫammurapi ha giurato.
16. _igi_ an-pi4-{d}a-a _sanga {d}utu_ 
#tr.it: Dinnanzi a Anpi-ayya, supervisore del personale del tempio,
17. _igi#_ isz-me-{d}suen _sanga {d}utu_ 
#tr.it: dinnanzi a Išmi-sin, supervisore del personale del tempio,
18. [_igi_] {d}marduk-la-ma-sa3-szu _ugula lukur utu_ 
#tr.it: dinnanzi a Marduk-lamassašu, supervisore delle naditu di Šamaš,
19. [_igi_ ra]-pa#-asz-MI{li2}-e2-a _ugula lukur utu_  
#tr.it: dinnanzi a Rapaš-ṣilli, supervisore delle naditu di Šamaš,
20. [_igi_ x]-x-{d}en-lil2 
#tr.it: dinnanzi a ...-enlil,
21. [_igi_ x-x]-ma-an-szum2 
#tr.it: dinnanzi a ...manšum,
22. [_igi_ e]-ri#-ib-{d}suen 
#tr.it: dinnanzi a Erib-sin.
@left 
1. [_iti_] e#-lu-lu _u4 1(u) 3(disz)-kam_ 
#tr.it: Il mese di Elelu, il giorno 13,
2. [_mu_] esz3#-nun-na _a gal-gal mu-un-gul-la_
#tr.it: (del)l'anno (in cui) Ešunna dall'inondazione fu distrutta.

&P382524 = CT 02, pl. 43, Bu 1891-05-09, 2175a 
#atf: lang akk 
@tablet 
@obverse 
1. {disz}hu-za-lum u3 KA-{d}a-a _lukur_ {d}utu
#tr.ts: ḫuzalum u pî-ayya nadīt šamaš
#tr.en: Ḫuzalum and Pî-ayya nadītu of Šamaš,
2. _dumu-me_ na-bi-{d}utu 
#tr.ts: mārū nabi-šamaš
#tr.en: sons of Nabi-šamaš,
3. asz-szum _igi-sa2_ la-ma-sa3-at {d}inanna sza _ga2#-[gi-a]{ki}_ 
#tr.ts: aššum igisîm lama(s)sat ištar ša gagîm
#tr.en: on account of the (annual) tax to the statue of Ištar in (lit. of) the cloister
4. is,-s,a-ab-tu {disz}{d}suen-na-di-in-szu-mi 
#tr.ts: iṣṣabtu sîn-nādin-šumī
#tr.en: that was taken, Sîn-nādin-šumī,
5. sza-pi2-ir zimbir{ki} _di-ku5-mesz_ ik-szu-du!-ma 
#tr.ts: šāpir sippar dayyānī ikšudūma
#tr.en: the governor of Sippar, (and) the judges have approached
6. a-wa-ti-szu-nu i-mu-ru-ma 
#tr.ts: awātīšunu īmurūma
#tr.en: so they have investigated their case and:
7. _3(disz) sila3 ninda e2_ {d}utu a-na _2(disz) sila3 ninda-ta_ tu-ur-ru 
#tr.ts: šalāšat qa akal bīt šamaš ana šina qa akalim turru
#tr.en: 3 litres of bread (from ?) the temple of Šamaš reduced to 2 litres of bread,
8. _6(disz) sila3 kasz 2(disz) {dug}bur-zi utu2 1(disz) {dug}bur-de2-a_ 
#tr.ts: šeššet qa šikaram šittā pursâtim diktim ištēn pūram nāqiam
#tr.en: 6 litres of beer, 2 bowls of dairy, 1 platter,
9. 2(disz) mi-sze-er-tim _uzu szu!-ti-a_ {disz}hu-za-lum 
#tr.ts: šittā mīšertim šīrim namḫartim ḫuzalum
#tr.en: 2 cuts of meat received by Ḫuzalum (as a prerogative)
10. sza sza-ta-mu-ti-szu sza _e2_ {d}utu 
#tr.ts: ša šata(m)mūtīšu ša bīt šamaš
#tr.en: of his status as accountant in the temple of Šamaš
11. i-na _iti 1(disz)-kam u4 6(disz)-kam 2(disz) sila3 kasz_ sza ki-di-im 
#tr.ts: ina ištēn warḫim šeššet ūmī šinā qa šikaram ša kīdim
#tr.en: for one month and six days, 2 litres of beer from outside
12. i-s,a-am u3 ma-dam u2-pa-hi-ru-ma 
#tr.ts: īṣam u mādam upa(ḫ)ḫirūma
#tr.en: they have collected everything and
13. _7(disz) gin2 ku3-babbar igi-sa2_ la-ma-sa3-at {d}inanna 
#tr.ts: sebet šiqil kaspim igisîm lama(s)sat ištar
#tr.en: (on:) 7 shekels of silver, the (annual) tax for the statue of Ištar,
14. _7(asz) 3(barig) sze gur ninda_ u3 _kasz_ qa2-du-um 
#tr.ts: sebet kur šalāšat pān îm akalim u šikarim qadum
#tr.en: 2.280 litres of barley bread and beer together with
15. _3(asz) sze gur_ sza isz-tu _iri_ sza3-ga{ki?} 
#tr.ts: šalāšat kur îm ša ištu āli šaga
#tr.en: 900 litres of barley, which from the city of Šaga
16. il-la-qe2-a-am mi-il-qe2-<et> {disz}hu-za-lum <a>-hi-sza 
#tr.ts: illaqiam milqēt ḫuzalum aḫīša
#tr.en: was taken, the income of Ḫuzalum her brother
17. sza KA-{d}a-a il-te-qu2-u2 
#tr.ts: ša pî-ayya ilteqû
#tr.en: that Pî-ayya had taken,
18. i-na _ka2 ga2-gi-a{ki}_ 
#tr.ts: ina bāb gagîm
#tr.en: at the gate of the cloister
19. {disz}KA#-[{d}]a#-a# u3# hu-za-lum 
#tr.ts: pî-ayya u ḫuzalum
#tr.en: Pî-ayya and Ḫuzalum
20. sza im-ta-ag-ru-u2-ma 
#tr.ts: ša imtagrūma
#tr.en: have come to an agreement and,
@reverse 
1. i-na mi-it-gu-ur-ti-szu-nu 
#tr.ts: ina mitgurtīšunu
#tr.en: in full agreement,
2. i-na _7(disz) gin2 ku3-babbar igi-sa2_ la-ma-sa3-at {d}inanna 
#tr.ts: ina sebet šiqil kaspim igisîm lama(s)sat ištar
#tr.en: with: 7 shekels of silver, the (annual) tax for the statue of Ištar (of which)
3. _5(disz) gin2 ku3-babbar_ ki-is,-ru? sza KA-{d}a-[a] x-ru-um?-ma 
#tr.ts: ḫamšat šiqil kaspim kiṣru(m) ša pî-ayya ...
#tr.en: 5 shekels of silver, the rent that Pî-ayya ... and
4. _2(disz) gin2 ku3-babbar_ szi-ta-at _igi-sa2_ 
#tr.ts: šinā šiqil kaspim šītat igisîm
#tr.en: 2 shekels of silver, the remainder of the (annual) tax,
5. _6(asz) 3(barig) sze gur_ sza _ninda kasz_ 
#tr.ts: šeššet kur šalāšat pān îm ša akalim šikarim
#tr.en: 1.980 litres of bread and beer
6. {disz}KA-{d}a-a _dumu-munus_ na-bi-{d}utu 
#tr.ts: pî-ayya mārat nabi-šamaš
#tr.en: Pî-ayya, daughter of Nabi-šamaš,
7. a#-na# hu-za-lum a-ha-sza i-pu-ul# 
#tr.ts: ana ḫuzalum aḫāša īpul
#tr.en: has satisfied Ḫuzalum her brother (so)
8. ru-gu-me-szu is-su2-uh 
#tr.ts: rugu(m)mêšu issuḫ
#tr.en: he has renounced his claim.
9. u2-ul i-ta-ar-ma {disz}hu-za-lum 
#tr.ts: ul itârma ḫuzalum
#tr.en: (That) again Ḫuzalum,
10. a-na _7(disz) gin2 ku3-babbar igi-sa2_ la#-ma#-si2 {d}inanna 
#tr.ts: ana sebet šiqil kaspim igisîm lama(s)si ištar
#tr.en: regarding the 7 shekels of silver, the (annual) tax for the statue of Ištar,
11. u3 _6(asz) 3(barig) sze gur_ sza _ninda_ u3 _kasz_ 
#tr.ts: u šeššet kur šalāšat pān îm ša akalim šikarim
#tr.en: and the 1.980 litres of bread and beer,
12. a-na KA-{d}a-a _dumu-munus_ na-bi-{d}utu a-ha-ta-szu 
#tr.ts: ana pî-ayya mārat nabi-šamaš aḫātašu
#tr.en: against Pî-ayya, daughter of Nabi-šamaš his sister,
13. u2-ul i-ra-ga-am 
#tr.ts: ul ira(g)gam
#tr.en: not raise a claim
14. _mu_ {d}utu {d}a-a {d}marduk 
#tr.ts: nīš šamaš ayya marduk
#tr.en: by the life of Šamaš, Ayya, Marduk
15. u3 sa-am-su-i-lu-na _lugal-e_ it-mu-u2 
#tr.ts: u samsu-iluna šarrim itmû
#tr.en: and Samsu-iluna the king they have sworn.
$ single ruling 
16. _igi_ {d}marduk-ni-szu 
#tr.ts: maḫar marduk-nīšu
#tr.en: Before Marduk-nīšu (and)
17. _igi_ ra-pa-asz-s,il2-li2-e2-a _ugula-mesz lukur_ {d}utu 
#tr.ts: maḫar rapaš-ṣilli-ea aklī nadiāt šamaš
#tr.en: before Rapaš-ṣilli-ea, the overseers of Šamaš’s Nadītu's;
18. _igi_ a-wi-il-{d}iszkur _dub-sar lukur {d}utu-mesz_ 
#tr.ts: maḫar awīl-adad ṭupšar nadiāt šamaš
#tr.en: before Awīl-adad, the scribe of Šamaš’s Nadītu's;
19. _igi_ lu-sza-lim-be-li2 sza _lukur {d}utu-mesz_ 
#tr.ts: maḫar lu-šalim-bēlī ša nadiātim šamaš
#tr.en: before Lu-šalim-bēlī of Šamaš’s Nadītu's.
20. _iti sig4-a u4 2(u) 1(disz)-kam_ 
#tr.ts: waraḫ simānim ūmam ešrā ištēn
#tr.en: The month of Simānum, the day 21
21. _mu_ sa-am-su-i-lu-na _lugal-e alan {gesz}tukul! sig3-ge e2!-sag-il2-la mu-un-na-a_ 
#tr.ts: šattum ša samsu-iluna šarrum ṣalmam kakkam māḫiṣam ina esagila īpušu
#tr.en: the year in which Samsu-iluna the king made a statue (representing himself) wielding a weapon in the Esagila.

&P382525 = CT 02, pl. 47, Bu 1891-05-09, 2182 
#atf: lang akk 
@tablet 
@obverse 
1. a-na _1/3(disz) sar e2 du3-a_ sza ga-gi-im
#tr.ts: ana šaluš mūšar bītim epšim ša gagîm
#tr.en: For: the built house plot of 20 shekels in the cloister
2. sza _da e2_ la-ma-si2 
#tr.ts: ša ṭēḫi bīt lama(s)si
#tr.en: that is next to the house of Lamassi,
3. {disz}{munus}be-el-tum _e2_ a-bi bu-sze-e! u2!(pa)-ni-a-tim 
# coll. Ferwerda
#tr.ts: bēltum bīt abi būšê uniatim
#tr.en: Bēltum of the paternal house, moveables and utensils
4. sza geme2-{d}utu _dumu-munus_ su-pa-pu-um# 
#tr.ts: ša amat-šamaš mārat supapum
#tr.en: that Amat-šamaš, daughter of Supapum,
5. a-na _dumu-munus_ sin-e-ri-ba-am 
#tr.ts: ana mārat sîn-erībam
#tr.en: to the daughter of Sîn-erībam,
6. _dumu-munus-a-ni_ id-di-nu 
#tr.ts: mārtīša iddinu
#tr.en: her (adoptive) daughter, had given,
7. {disz}ni-id-nu-sza u3 {d}utu-a-pi2-li 
#tr.ts: nidnuša u šamaš-āpilī
#tr.en: Nidnuša and Šamaš-āpilī
8. _dumu-mesz!(MUNUS)_ id-di-nu-nim 
#tr.ts: mārū iddinunim
#tr.en: sons of Iddinunim
9. a-na _dumu-munus_ sin-e-ri-ba-am 
#tr.ts: ana mārat sîn-erībam
#tr.en: against the daughter of Sîn-erībam
10. ir-gu-mu-u2-ma um-ma szu-nu-u2-ma 
#tr.ts: irgumūma umma šunūma
#tr.en: have made a claim and they:
11. mi-im-ma geme2-{d}utu _e2_ u2-ul id-di-na-ki 
#tr.ts: mimma amat-šamaš bītim ul iddinaki
#tr.en: “No estate Amat-šamaš gave you
12. u3 t,up-pa-am u2-ul isz-t,u2-ra-ki-im 
#tr.ts: u ṭuppam ul išṭurakim
#tr.en: and a document did not write for you.
13. i-na mi-tu-ti-sza-a-ma 
#tr.ts: ina mītūtīšāma
#tr.en: After her death
14. at-ti-i-ma ta-asz-t,u2-ri 
#tr.ts: attīma tašṭuri
#tr.en: you wrote yourself!”
15. ki-a-am iq-bu-u2-ma 
#tr.ts: kīam iqbūma
#tr.en: thus have said. So
16. {disz}su-mu-akszak{ki} im-hu-ru-u2-ma 
#tr.ts: sumu-akšak imḫrūma
#tr.en: they have approached Sumu-akšak and
17. a-na szi-bi-sza u3 szi-ba-ti-sza 
#tr.ts: ana šībīša u šībātīša
#tr.en: for (taking the testimony of) her witnesses, men and women,
18. _szu-nir_ sza {d}utu 
#tr.ts: šurinnum ša šamaš
#tr.en: the emblem of Šamaš,
19. sza-sza-rum sza {d}utu 
#tr.ts: ša(š)šārum ša šamaš
#tr.en: the saw of Šamaš,
20. ba-asz-mu-um sza esz-har-ra 
#tr.ts: bašmum ša ešḫarra
#tr.en: (and) the “bašmu” snake of Ešḫarra,
@reverse 
1. a-na ga-gi-im i-ru-bu-ma 
#tr.ts: ana gagîm īrubūma
#tr.en: have entered the cloister and
2. szi-bu-sza u3 szi-ba-tu-sza 
#tr.ts: šībūša u šībātūša
#tr.en: her witnesses, men and women,
3. sza i-na bu-ul-t,i3-sza-a-ma 
#tr.ts: ša ina bulṭīšāma
#tr.en: that during her lifetime (of Amat-šamaš)
4. _e2_ id-di-nu u3 t,up-pa-am isz-t,u2-ru 
#tr.ts: bītam iddinu u ṭuppam išṭuru
#tr.en: had given the house and written a document,
5. iq-bu-u2-ma _di-ku5-mesz_ 
#tr.ts: iqbūma dayyānū
#tr.en: have declared so the judges
6. di-nam u2-sza-hi-zu-szu-nu-ti-ma 
#tr.ts: dīnam ušāḫizūšunūtīma
#tr.en: have brought them (Nidnuša and Šamaš-āpilī) to trial and
7. _di-ku5-<mesz>_ a-na ar-na e-mi-di-szu 
#tr.ts: dayyānū ana arna(m) emēdīšu
#tr.en: the judges, to punish him (Nidnuša)
8. iq-bu-u2-ma _di-ku5 tug2?_-su2? e-li-szu id-di 
#tr.ts: iqbūma dayyānum ṣubā(s)su elīšu iddi
#tr.en: have decreed and the judge has cast his garment on him.
9. u2-ul i-tu-ru-u2-ma 
#tr.ts: ul itū(r)rūma
#tr.en: Anew,
10. {disz}ni-id-nu-sza {d}utu-a-pi2-li 
#tr.ts: nidnuša šamaš-āpilī
#tr.en: Nidnuša, Šamaš-āpilī
11. u3 a-ah-hu-sza sza geme2-{d}utu ma-la bi#!-it#! bu-sze-e! u2!(pa)-ni-a-tim 
#tr.ts: u aḫḫūša ša amat-šamaš mala bīt būšê uniatim
#tr.en: and the (lit. her) brothers of Amat-šamaš, any of as much, house, moveables and utensils
12. i-ba-asz-szu-u2 a-na _dumu-munus_ sin-e-ri-ba-am 
#tr.ts: ibaššū ana mārat sîn-erībam
#tr.en: as there are, on the daughter of Sîn-erībam
