>>Q000628 048 
#tr.en: To the house(?) where the righteous man raised (his) hand. 
49. a-bi lu2-zi-de3 szu bi2-in-e3-ba-a-sze3 
>>Q000628 049 
#tr.en: To that house(?) where the righteous man raised (his) hand. 
50. mu-lu-bi e2-sza3-ga {mu}nu2 gi-rin-ne bi2-in-ak 
>>Q000628 050 
#tr.en: In the Ešag that man set up a bed in flowers. 
51. e2-an-na-ka gada-la2-e! na ba-e-na-ag2 
>>Q000628 051 
#tr.en: In the House-of-Heaven the linen-clad erected(?) a stone(?) for him. 
52. u3-mu-un-ra a mu-un-ma-al mu-na-ab-be2-ne 
>>Q000628 052 
#tr.en: Addressing the lord, water was prepared. 
53. ninda{+en-da} mu-un-ma-al mu-un-na-ab-be2-ne 
>>Q000628 053 
#tr.en: Addressing him, bread was prepared. 
54. e2-gal-la NI2-te-en mu-un-na-ab-be2-ne 
>>Q000628 054 
#tr.en: They are telling him to refresh in the palace. 
55. {d}dumu-zi e2-e-am3 ki-am3 u4-zalag-ga 
>>Q000628 055 
#tr.en: O Dumuzi, it is in(?) the house, a place bright as a day it is. 
56. ama {d}inanna ama {d}inanna du6-zu du-zu 
>>Q000628 056 
#tr.en: Mother Inanna, Mother Inanna, your hill(?), your going(?). 
57. ama {d}inanna {d}inanna-an-na tug2-zu tug2-zu 
>>Q000628 057 
#tr.en: Mother Inanna, Inanna-of-Heaven, your clothes, your clothes. 
58. tug2-gi6-zu tug2-babbar-zu 
>>Q000628 058 
#tr.en: Your black clothes, your white clothes. 
59. mu-lu e2-a gen-na-mu te-e-am3 
>>Q000628 059 
#tr.en: It is indeed(?) my man who strolled around the house. 
60. i-lu te-am3 ad-sza4-sza3-ba 
>>Q000628 060 
#tr.en: It is indeed(?) a song, a heart’s lament. 
61. me-e-bi te-am3 me ba-tusz-u3-ne 
>>Q000628 061 
#tr.en: Its me it is indeed. They (shall) place the me. 
62. ki-bi te-am3 ki am3-gub-bu-ne 
>>Q000628 062 
#tr.en: Its place it is indeed. They (shall) set the (proper) place. 
63. am3-mi-in-gub-bu-ne am3-mi-in-gub-bu-ne 
>>Q000628 063 
#tr.en: They (shall) place him, they (shall) place him. 
64. {d}mu-ul-lil2 ki-ur3!-ra am3-mi-in-gub-bu-ne 
>>Q000628 064 
#tr.en: They (shall) place Enlil in the ki’ur. 
65. am szi-ka-na-ag2-ga2 mu-lu2-bi de3-en-ti 
>>Q000628 065 
#tr.en: O lord, life of the land, I will revive that man. 
66. em3 ni2-bi em3 ni2-bi de3-ak 
>>Q000628 066 
#tr.en: I will make things alone(?), things alone(?). 
67. lu2-bi e2-nun-na KA inim-si-sa2 de3-bi2-in-ak 
>>Q000628 067 
#tr.en: For its men I will make a firm promise in the cella. 
68. a-ga-e2-gal-la2-ka inim-si-sa2 im-be2-en-na 
>>Q000628 068 
#tr.en: (Whatever) it is that you say as firm promise in the rear part of the palace. 
69. in-nin9 ubur-zu gan2-ne2-zu he2-a 
>>Q000628 069 
#tr.en: O Inanna, your breast is indeed your field. 
70. {d}inanna ubur-zu gan2-ne2-zu he2-a 
>>Q000628 070 
#tr.en: O Inanna, your breast is indeed your field. 
71. gan2-ne2 dagal-e gu de2-a-zu 
>>Q000628 071 
#tr.en: When you poured out flax in the wide field. 
72. gan2-ne2 dagal-e sze de2-a-zu 
>>Q000628 072 
#tr.en: When you poured out barley in the wide field. 
73. a bala-am3-ta mu-lu2 SZE gar-am3-ta 
>>Q000628 073 
#tr.en: (Then) draw water from there (and) establish(?) it for the men! 
74. a bala-bala-am3-ta mu-lu2 gar-gar-am3-ta 
>>Q000628 074 
#tr.en: Draw much water from there (and) establish it plentifully for the men! 
75. mu-lu du11-ga-ra u3-na-e-ni-du11 
>>Q000628 075 
#tr.en: After you have told it the man addressed, 
76. ne-en ga-ra-na8-na8? 
>>Q000628 076 
#tr.en: I will drink that on your behalf(?). 
77. szir3-nam-szub-{d}inanna-kam 
#tr.en: It is an incantation-song of Inanna, 
>>Q000628 colophon 
78. 1(gesz2) 1(u) 6(disz) mu?-bi?-im? 
#tr.en: 76 are its lines. 
>>Q000628 colophon

